    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **263 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event on the owner-create pipeline's audit step.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **New immutable event type** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` (a Java `record`, so it can't be mutated after construction) with fields in spec order: `seq`, `ownerId`, `customerCode`, `membershipLevel`, `event`, plus the `OWNER_CREATED` constant.\n\n2. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 after the existing human-readable audit line, it now also serializes an `OwnerCreatedEvent` to JSON and logs it to the same `AUDIT` logger:\n   ```\n   {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n   ```\n   - `seq` comes from a static `AtomicLong` incremented once per create \u2192 **monotonically increasing across creates**.\n   - The identifier value is sourced through a single line: `String primaryIdentifier = owner.getCustomerCode();` \u2014 the owner's **current primary identifier**. When `customerCode` is later unified into `memberId`, only that one accessor changes and the event automatically carries the `memberId` instead, as the spec requires.\n   - Logged via `AUDIT.info(\"{}\", json)` so SLF4J emits the JSON verbatim rather than interpreting its braces.\n\n**Design notes:**\n- Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson`) is the app's mapper, and its serialization exceptions are unchecked, so no `throws` clause was needed \u2014 the function class keeps its single public method (per the OfficeFloor convention in AGENTS.md).\n- The existing `service` method retains its single-public-method shape; `OwnerCreatedEvent` is a plain record, not a wired function class.\n\nThe target acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier`) passes, and the full 263-test suite remains green.",
